# Everything under astroos/ is a build input consumed on Linux: shell scripts,
# alpm hooks, systemd units, pacman configuration, kernel configs and patches.
# A CRLF checkout breaks them, and where a file is covered by a checksum it
# breaks the checksum too: astroos/pkgs/linux-astroos/config is pinned by a
# b2sum in its PKGBUILD, so a single stray carriage return fails the build.
#
# text=auto lets git detect binaries (the branding PNGs, the vendored fonts)
# and leave them exactly as they are; eol=lf pins the working copy for the
# rest, on Windows as well as on the build host.
astroos/** text=auto eol=lf
*.patch    text=auto eol=lf
*.PKGBUILD text=auto eol=lf
PKGBUILD   text=auto eol=lf
